    "title": "Backstage Update - MJF's AEW Status - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Clark ,\n4 minutes ago\nMJF is expected to return to AEW television “soon,” following his hiatus to focus on acting projects.\nEarlier this month, it was reported that the former AEW World Champion was close to finishing filming Violent Night 2 . At that time, there was no clear update on when he would be back in AEW. However, Fightful Select is now reporting that sources within AEW say MJF’s return is coming “soon,” though no exact date has been provided.\nREAD MORE: Injury Update On Buddy Matthews\nREAD MORE: Injury Update On Queen Aminata\nDuring his time away, MJF has stayed active in Hollywood, filming both Violent Night 2 and Happy Gilmore 2 . According to the report, he has “really enjoyed” acting and intends to continue pursuing roles while balancing his wrestling schedule.\nMJF’s last AEW match took place at All Out 2025, where he lost to Mark Briscoe. AEW has creative plans for MJF in December, though it remains unclear how frequently he will appear on television. He is also confirmed to appear at WrestleCade, which runs from November 28th through November 30th.\nNOTE: If you have any news tips or podcast recaps that you’d like to send in for us to post (full credit will be given to you), please email me at RClarkPWS@Yahoo.com .",
